  "entry": "code/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Flag which candidate compounds carry a classic Type II heme-coordinating motif (imidazole, triazole, pyridine, thiazole) for CYP450 inhibition, and show, for four cryo-EM reference compounds only, precomputed Boltz-2 predictions of whether the motif nitrogen actually coordinates the heme iron. The structural check is a fixed, checked-in four-compound summary; it is not run on compounds the user screens, and none of the blinded challenge compounds have it yet. Data used in the run: stock. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
